//? Title: PointNet:genuine CAD points and visible tensor Adam
//? Subtitle: Tensor computations, explicit checks and reproducible local figures
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Original CAD surface observations feed the complete PointNet graph. Every tensor Adam update,paired population-BN checkpoint and held-out object error is visible alongside source geometry and invariance limits.
)
\toc

Source example: `examples/cpp/source/nn/1_convolutional_neural_networks/1.10_3d_and_video_convolutions/pointnet.cpp`.

> The method

Use actual sampled ModelNet surfaces,keep every source layer,and show the optimizer objective and update directly. Select matching learned/moving arrays on validation,restore XYZ-only inference,and report every held-out object and ordering control.

The editable concept diagram is `diagrams/pointnet_concept.tikz`. Regeneration uses
LaTeX with PGF/TikZ and standalone, plus dvisvgm; exports use the saved SVG.

```{bash, results="output", file="figures/pointnet_concept.svg"}
set -eu
mkdir -p build
latex -interaction=batchmode -halt-on-error -output-directory=build diagrams/pointnet_concept.tikz > build/pointnet_concept.compile.log 2>&1
dvisvgm --no-fonts --bbox=10 --output=build/pointnet_concept.svg build/pointnet_concept.dvi > build/pointnet_concept.render.log 2>&1
printf 'Rendered local concept diagram.\n'
```
